{
  "title": "29: al-Ankaboot العنكبوت",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nالٓمّٓ‌ ۚ‏(1)\nALIF LAAAM MEEM.\nAlif Lam Meem (A. L. M.).\nاَحَسِبَ النَّاسُ اَنْ يُّتْرَكُوْۤا اَنْ يَّقُوْلُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا وَهُمْ لَا يُفْتَنُوْنَ‏(2)\nA-HASEBAN NAASO ANY YUTRAKOO ANY YAQOOLOO AAMAANNAA WA HUM LAA YUFTANOON.\nWhat! Do people imagine that they will be left off on (their) saying: “We believe!” and they will not be tried?\nوَلَقَدْ فَتَنَّا الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ‌ فَلَيَعْلَمَنَّ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ صَدَقُوْا وَلَيَعْلَمَنَّ الْكٰذِبِيْنَ‏(3)\nWA LAQAD FATANNAL LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM FA-LA-YA’LAMANNAL LAAHUL LAZEENA SADAQOO WA LA-YA’LAMANNAL KAAZEBEEN.\nAnd indeed We did try those before them, so God certainly knoweth those who are true, and certainly knoweth He the liars.\nاَمْ حَسِبَ الَّذِيْنَ يَعْمَلُوْنَ السَّيِّاٰتِ اَنْ يَّسْبِقُوْنَا‌ ؕ سَآءَ مَا يَحْكُمُوْنَ‏(4)\nAM HASEBAL LAZEENA YA’MALOONAS SAYYEAATE ANY YASBEQOONAA, SAAA-A MAA YAHKOMOON.\nOr imagine they who work evil that they will escape Us? Ill it is what they judge.\nمَنْ كَانَ يَرْجُوْا لِقَآءَ اللّٰهِ فَاِنَّ اَجَلَ اللّٰهِ لَاٰتٍ‌ؕ وَهُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(5)\nMAN KAANA YARJOO LE-QAAA-AL LAAHE FA-INNA AJALAL LAAHE LA-AAT, WA HOWAS SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nWhoever hopeth to meet God and then verily the doom decreed by God shall certainly come (to pass); and He is the All Hearing, the All-Knowing.\nوَمَنْ جَاهَدَ فَاِنَّمَا يُجَاهِدُ لِنَفْسِهٖؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَغَنِىٌّ عَنِ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(6)\nWA MAN JAAHADA FA-INNAMAA YOJAAHEDO LE-NAFSEH, INNAL LAAHA LA-GHANIYYUN A’NIL A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd whoever striveth hard, he striveth only for his own self; verily God is Self- Sufficient (Independent of the needs) of (all) the worlds.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ لَنُكَفِّرَنَّ عَنْهُمْ سَيِّاٰتِهِمْ وَلَنَجْزِيَنَّهُمْ اَحْسَنَ الَّذِىْ كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(7)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE LA-NOKAFFERANNA A’NHUM SAYYEAATEHIM WA LANAJZEYANNAHUM AHSANAL LAZEE KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nAnd (as to) those who believe and do good, certainly will We blot out from them their evil deeds and certainly will We recompense them the best of what they were doing.\nوَوَصَّيْنَا الْاِنْسَانَ بِوَالِدَيْهِ حُسْنًا‌ ؕ وَاِنْ جَاهَدٰكَ لِتُشْرِكَ بِىْ مَا لَيْسَ لَكَ بِهٖ عِلْمٌ فَلَا تُطِعْهُمَا ؕ اِلَىَّ مَرْجِعُكُمْ فَاُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(8)\nWA WASSAYNAL INSAANA BE-WAALEDAYHE HUSNAA, WA IN JAAHADAAKA LE-TUSHREKA BEE MAA LAYSA LAKA BEHI I’LMUN FALAA TO-TE’HOMAA, ELAYYA MARJE-O’KUM FA-ONABBE-OKUM BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nAnd We have enjoined on man goodness unto his parents; and if they (either of them) strive (to force) thee to associate (others) with Me (in worship) of which thou hast no knowledge, then thou obey them not; Unto Me is the return of ye (all) and then will I inform you of what ye were doing.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ لَنُدْخِلَنَّهُمْ فِى الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(9)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE LANUDKHELANNAHUM FIS SAALEHEEN.\nAnd those who believe and do good, certainly We will admit them among the righteous,\nوَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَّقُوْلُ اٰمَنَّا بِاللّٰهِ فَاِذَاۤ اُوْذِىَ فِى اللّٰهِ جَعَلَ فِتْنَةَ النَّاسِ كَعَذَابِ اللّٰهِؕ وَلَئِنْ جَآءَ نَصْرٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ لَيَقُوْلُنَّ اِنَّا كُنَّا مَعَكُمْ‌ؕ اَوَلَيْسَ اللّٰهُ بِاَعْلَمَ بِمَا فِىْ صُدُوْرِ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(10)\nWA MENAN NAASE MANY YAQOOLO AAMANNAA BIL LAAHE FA-EZAA OOZEYA FIL LAAHE JA-A’LA FITNATAN NAASE KA-A’ZAABIL LAAH, WA LAIN JAAA-A NASRUM MIR RABBEKA LA-YAQOOLUNNA INNAA KUNNAA MA-A’KUM, AWA LAYSAL LAAHO BE-A’ALAMA BEMAA FEE SODOORIL A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd among the people are those who say: “We believe in God;” and when they are persecuted in the (way of) God they think the persecution from the people as the chastisement from God; and yet if cometh the help from thy Lord they would certainly say: “Verily, we were with you:” What! is not God the Best-Knower of what is in the breast of all those in (His own created) worlds?\nوَلَيَعْلَمَنَّ اللّٰهُ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَلَيَعْلَمَنَّ الْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ‏(11)\nWA LA-YA’LAMANAL LAAHUL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA LA-YA’LAMANNAL MONAAFEQEEN.\nAnd certainly well-knoweth God those who believe and certainly well-knoweth He the hypocrites.\nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا اتَّبِعُوْا سَبِيْلَنَا وَلْنَحْمِلْ خَطٰيٰكُمْ ؕ وَمَا هُمْ بِحٰمِلِيْنَ مِنْ خَطٰيٰهُمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ‌ؕ اِنَّهُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(12)\nWA QAALAL LAZEENA KAFAROO LIL-LAZEENA AAMANUT TABE-O’O SABEELANAA WAL NAHMIL KHATAAYAAKUM, WA MAA HUM BE-HAAMELEENA MIN KHATAAYAAHUM MIN SHAY, INNAHUM LA-KAAZEBOON.\nAnd those who disbelieve say unto those who believe; “Follow ye our path and we will certainly bear (the burden of) your sins.” And they shall not be bearers of any thing of their sins; Verily, they are liars.\nوَلَيَحْمِلُنَّ اَ ثْقَالَهُمْ وَاَ ثْقَالًا مَّعَ اَثْقَالِهِمْ‌ وَلَيُسْئَلُنَّ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ عَمَّا كَانُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(13)\nWA LAYAHMELUNNA ASQAALAHUM WA ASQAALAM MA-A’ ASQAALEHIM, WA LA-YUS-ALUNNA YAWMAL QEYAAMATE A’MMAA KAANOO YAFTAROON.\nAnd certainly they shall bear their own burdens, and (other) burdens with their own burdens, and certainly, shall they be questioned on the Day of Judgment as to what they were forging.\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا نُوْحًا اِلٰى قَوْمِهٖ فَلَبِثَ فِيْهِمْ اَ لْفَ سَنَةٍ اِلَّا خَمْسِيْنَ عَامًا ؕ فَاَخَذَهُمُ الطُّوْفَانُ وَهُمْ ظٰلِمُوْنَ‏(14)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA NOOHAN ELAA QAWMEHI FALABESA FEEHIM ALFA SANATIN ILLAA KHAMSEENA A’AMAA, FA-AKHAZNAAHOMUT TOOFAANO WA HUM ZAALEMOON.\nAnd indeed sent We Noah unto his people, and he did stay amidst them a thousand years but fifty years; and seized them the Deluge while they were unjust.\nفَاَنْجَيْنٰهُ وَاَصْحٰبَ السَّفِيْنَةِ وَجَعَلْنٰهَاۤ اٰيَةً لِّلْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(15)\nFA-ANJAYNAAHO WA ASHAABAS SAFEENATE WA JA-A’LNAAHAA AAYATAL LIL-A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd We delivered him and the inmates of the Ark, and We made it a sign unto the people of the worlds.\nوَاِبْرٰهِيْمَ اِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ وَاتَّقُوْهُ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكُمْ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(16)\nWA IBRAAHEEMA IZ QAALA LE-QAWMEHI’ BODUL LAAHA WAT-TAQOOH, ZAALEKUM KHAYRUL LAKUM IN KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nAnd (recollect) Abraham when he said unto his people; “Worship ye God and fear Him; This is best for you, if ye but know.\nاِنَّمَا تَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اَوْثَانًا وَّتَخْلُقُوْنَ اِفْكًا‌ ؕ اِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ تَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ لَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ لَكُمْ رِزْقًا فَابْتَغُوْا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ الرِّزْقَ وَاعْبُدُوْهُ وَاشْكُرُوْا لَهٗ ؕ اِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(17)\nINNAMAA TA’BODOONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE AWSAANANW WA TAKHLOQOONA IFKAA, INNAL LAZEENA TA’BODOONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE LAA YAMLEKOONA LAKUM RIZQAN FAB-TAGHOO I’NDAL LAAHIR RIZQA WA’BODOOHO WASH KOROO LAH, ELAYHE TURJA-O’ON.\nYe only worship idols besides God, and create a lie; verily those whom ye worship besides God, own not for you any sustenance, so seek ye from God (your) sustenance and worship ye (only) Him, and give ye thanks (only) unto Him; unto Him (only) shall ye (all) be returned.\nوَاِنْ تُكَذِّبُوْا فَقَدْ كَذَّبَ اُمَمٌ مِّنْ قَبْلِكُمْ‌ؕ وَمَا عَلَى الرَّسُوْلِ اِلَّا الْبَلٰغُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(18)\nWA IN TOKAZZEBOO FAQAD KAZZABA OMAMUM MIN QABLEKUM, WA MAA A’LAR RASOOLE ILLAL BALAAGHUL MOBEEN.\nAnd if ye belie (the truth)! then indeed did belie (the truth) the people before you; and nothing is incumbent on the Apostle but a clear delivery (of the message).\nاَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا كَيْفَ يُبْدِئُ اللّٰهُ الْخَلْقَ ثُمَّ يُعِيْدُهٗ ؕ اِنَّ ذٰ لِكَ عَلَى اللّٰهِ يَسِيْرٌ‏(19)\nAWA LAM YARAW KAYFA YUBDEUL LAAHUL KHALQA SUMMA YO-E’EDOH, INNA ZAALEKA A’LAL LAAHE YASEER.\nWhat! see they not? How God originateth the creation then causeth it to return again? Verily this is easy for God.\nقُلْ سِيْرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ فَانْظُرُوْا كَيْفَ بَدَاَ الْخَلْقَ‌ ثُمَّ اللّٰهُ يُنْشِئُ النَّشْاَةَ الْاٰخِرَةَ‌ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‌ۚ‏(20)\nQUL SEEROO FIL ARZE FAN-ZOROO KAYFA BA-DA-AL KHALQA SUMMAL LAAHO YUNSHE-UN NASH-ATAL AAKHERAH, INNAL LAAHA A’LAA KULLE SHAYIN QADEER.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “Travel ye in the earth and see how He hath originated the creation so will God bringeth forth the later development (on the Day of Resurrection); Verily God hath power over all things.\nيُعَذِّبُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَرْحَمُ مَنْ يَّشَآءُ ‌ۚ وَاِلَيْهِ تُقْلَبُوْنَ‏(21)\nYO-A’ZZEBO MANY YASHAAA-O WA YARHAMO MANY YASHAAA, WA ELAYHE TUQLABOON.\nChastiseth He whomsoever He willeth and bestoweth mercy on whomsoever He willeth, and unto Him ye shall be turned back.\nوَمَاۤ اَنْتُمْ بِمُعْجِزِيْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَا فِى السَّمَآءِ‌ وَمَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مِنْ وَّلِىٍّ وَّلَا نَصِيْرٍ‏(22)\nWA MAA ANTUM BE-MO’JEZEENA FIL ARZE WA LAA FIS SAMAAA, WA MAA LAKUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE MINW WALIYYINW WA LAA NASEER.\nAnd ye shall frustrate not His power in the earth nor in the heaven, and there is not for you other than Him, any protector, nor a helper.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ وَلِقَآئِهٖۤ اُولٰٓئِكَ يَئِسُوْا مِنْ رَّحْمَتِىْ وَاُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(23)\nWAL LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-AAYAATIL LAAHE WA LEQAAA-EHI OOLAAA-EKA YA-ESOO MIR RAHMATEE WA OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nAnd those who disbelieved in the signs of God and His meeting, these are despaired of My mercy, and these it is who shall have a painful chastisement.\nفَمَا كَانَ جَوَابَ قَوْمِهٖۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ قَالُوا اقْتُلُوْهُ اَوْ حَرِّقُوْهُ فَاَنْجٰٮهُ اللّٰهُ مِنَ النَّارِ ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(24)\nFAMAA KAANA JAWAABA QAWMEHI ILLAAA AN QAALUQ TOLOOHO AW HARREQOOHO FA-ANJAAHUL LAAHO MENAN NAAR, INNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YOAMENOON.\nSo naught was the answer of his people except that they said: “Slay him or burn him;” Then God delivered him from the fire; verily in this there are signs for a people who believe.\nوَقَالَ اِنَّمَا اتَّخَذْتُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اَوْثَانًا ۙ مَّوَدَّةَ بَيْنِكُمْ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا ‌ۚ ثُمَّ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ يَكْفُرُ بَعْضُكُمْ بِبَعْضٍ وَّيَلْعَنُ بَعْضُكُمْ بَعْضًا  وَّمَاْوٰٮكُمُ النَّارُ وَمَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ نّٰصِرِيْنَ ۙ‏(25)\nWA QAALA INNAMAT TAKHAZTUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE AWSAANAM, MAWADDATA BAYNAKUM FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA, SUMMA YAWMAL QEYAAMATE YAKFORO BA’ZOHUM BE-BA’ZINW WA YAL-A’NO BA’ZOKUM BA’ZANW, WA MAAWAAKUMUN NAARO WA MAA LAKUM MIN NAASEREEN.\nAnd said (Abraham): “Ye have only taken for yourselves idols besides God in friendship between you in the life of this world, then on the Day of Judgment some of you shall deny the others, and shall curse some of you the others and your abode shall be the (Hell) fire, and for you shall not be any helpers,\nفَاٰمَنَ لَهٗ لُوْطٌ‌ۘ وَقَالَ اِنِّىْ مُهَاجِرٌ اِلٰى رَبِّىْ ؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(26)\nFA-AAMANA LAHU LOOT, WA QAALA INNEE MOHAAJERUN ELAA RABBEE, INNAHU HOWAL A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nThen believed in him Lut and said he: “I betake me unto my Lord, for verily He is the All-Mighty, the All-Wise\nوَوَهَبْنَا لَهٗۤ اِسْحٰقَ وَيَعْقُوْبَ وَجَعَلْنَا فِىْ ذُرِّيَّتِهِ النُّبُوَّةَ وَالْكِتٰبَ وَاٰتَيْنٰهُ اَجْرَهٗ فِى الدُّنْيَا ‌ۚ وَاِنَّهٗ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ لَمِنَ الصّٰلِحِيْنَ‏(27)\nWA WAHABNAA LAHU ISHAAQA WA YA’QOOBA WA JA-A’LNAA FEE ZURRIYYATEHIN NOBUWWATA WAL KETAABA WA AATAYNAAHO AJRAHU FID DUNYAA, WA INNAHU FIL AAKHERATE LAMENAS SAALEHEEN.\nAnd We granted him Isaac and Jacob, and made the prophethood and the Book to be in his seed, and We gave him his recompense in this world; and verily he in the hereafter will certainly be among the righteous ones.\nوَلُوْطًا اِذْ قَالَ لِقَوْمِهٖۤ اِنَّكُمْ لَتَاْتُوْنَ الْفَاحِشَةَ مَا سَبَقَكُمْ بِهَا مِنْ اَحَدٍ مِّنَ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(28)\nWA LOOTAN IZ QAALA LEQAWMEHI INNAKUM LA-TAATOONAL FAAHESHAH, MAA SABAQAKUM BEHAA MIN AHADIM MENAL A’ALAMEEN.\nAnd (recollect) Lut when said he unto his people: “Verily ye commit a lewdness, which not one of the people of the worlds gone before you did ever commit.\nاَئِنَّكُمْ لَتَاْتُوْنَ الرِّجَالَ وَتَقْطَعُوْنَ السَّبِيْلَ ۙ وَتَاْ تُوْنَ فِىْ نَادِيْكُمُ الْمُنْكَرَ ‌ؕ فَمَا كَانَ جَوَابَ قَوْمِهٖۤ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ قَالُوا ائْتِنَا بِعَذَابِ اللّٰهِ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏(29)\nA-INNAKUM LA-TAA-TOONAR REJAALA WA TAQTA-O’ONAS SABEEL, WA TAA-TOONA FEE NAADEEKOMUL MUNKAR, FAMAA KAANA JAWAABA QAWMEHI ILLAA AN QAALOO E-ATENAA BE-A’ZAABIL LAAHE IN KUNTA MENAS SAADEQEEN.\nWhat! Proceed ye unto men? and cut ye the highway (to plunder the wayfarers)? and commit ye evil deeds in your assemblies; But nothing was the answer from his people except that they said: “Bring thou unto us the chastisement from God, if thou art of the truthful (ones).\nقَالَ رَبِّ انْصُرْنِىْ عَلَى الْقَوْمِ الْمُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(30)\nQAALA RABBIN SURNEE A’LAL QAWMIL MUFSEDEEN.\nSaid (Lut): “O’ My Lord! Help me against the mischievous people!\nوَلَمَّا جَآءَتْ رُسُلُنَاۤ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ بِالْبُشْرٰىۙ قَالُوْۤا اِنَّا مُهْلِكُوْۤا اَهْلِ هٰذِهِ الْقَرْيَةِ ‌ۚ اِنَّ اَهْلَهَا كَانُوْا ظٰلِمِيْنَ‌ ۖ ‌ۚ‏(31)\nWA LAMMAA JAAA-AT ROSOLONAA IBRAAHEEMA BIL-BUSHRAA, QAALOO INNAA MOHLEKOO AHLE HAAZEHIL QARYAH, INNA AHLAHAA KAANOO ZAALEMEEN.\nAnd when came Our messengers unto Abraham with glad tidings (of a son unto him) said they: “Verily we are going to destroy the people of this town, for verily its people are unjust.\nقَالَ اِنَّ فِيْهَا لُوْطًا ‌ؕ قَالُوْا نَحْنُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنْ فِيْهَا‌ لَنُنَجِّيَنَّهٗ وَاَهْلَهٗۤ اِلَّا امْرَاَتَهٗ كَانَتْ مِنَ الْغٰبِرِيْنَ‏(32)\nQAALA INNA FEEHAA LOOTAA, QAALOO NAHNO A-A’LAMO BEMAN FEEHAA, LA-NONAJJE-YANNAHU WA AHLAHU ILLAM RA-ATAH, KAANAT MENAL GHAABEREEN.\nSaid (Abraham unto the messenger angels): “Verily in it is Lut.” They said: “We know it well who is in it; We shall certainly deliver him and his people; save his wife: she shall be of those who stay behind.\nوَلَمَّاۤ اَنْ جَآءَتْ رُسُلُنَا لُوْطًا سِىْٓءَ بِهِمْ وَضَاقَ بِهِمْ ذَرْعًا وَّقَالُوْا لَا تَخَفْ وَلَا تَحْزَنْ‌ اِنَّا مُنَجُّوْكَ وَاَهْلَكَ اِلَّا امْرَاَتَكَ كَانَتْ مِنَ الْغٰبِرِيْنَ‏(33)\nWA LAMMAA AN JAAA-AT ROSOLONAA LOOTAN SEEE-A BEHIM WA ZAAQA BEHIM ZAR-A’NW WA QAALOO LAA TAKHAF WA LAA TAHZAN, INNAA MONAJJOOKA WA AHLAKA ILLAM RA-ATAKA KAANAT MENAL GHAABEREEN.\nAnd when came Our Messengers unto Lut, he was grieved for them, and was straitened (at heart) for the (weakness of his) arm (to protect them): and they said “Fear thou not, nor grieve thou; verily we will deliver thee and thy people except thy wife; she shall be of those who stay behind.\nاِنَّا مُنْزِلُوْنَ عَلٰٓى اَهْلِ هٰذِهِ الْقَرْيَةِ رِجْزًا مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَفْسُقُوْنَ‏(34)\nINNAA MUNZELOONA A’LAA AHLE HAAZEHIL QARYAHTE RIJZAM MENAS SAMAAA-E BEMAA KAANOO YAFSOQOON.\nVerily We are bringing down upon the people of this town a punishment from heaven for what they were transgressing.\nوَلَقَد تَّرَكْنَا مِنْهَاۤ اٰيَةًۢ بَيِّنَةً لِّقَوْمٍ يَّعْقِلُوْنَ‏(35)\nWA LAQAD TARAKNAA MINHAA AAYATAM BAYYENATIL LEQAWMINY YA’QELOON.\nAnd indeed We have left a clear sign of it for a people who understand.\nوَاِلٰى مَدْيَنَ اَخَاهُمْ شُعَيْبًا ۙ فَقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ وَ ارْجُوا الْيَوْمَ الْاٰخِرَ وَلَا تَعْثَوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ مُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(36)\nWA ELAA MADYANA AKHAAHUM SHO-A’YBAA, FAQAALA YAA QAWME’ BODUL LAAHA WAR JUL YAWMAL AAKHERA WA LAA TA’SAW FIL ARZE MUFSEDEEN.\nAnd to Midian (We did send) their brother Shu’ayb and he said: “O’ my people! worship ye God (alone) and fear the Last day (of Judgment) and enact not evil in the earth making mischief (therein).\nفَكَذَّبُوْهُ فَاَخَذَتْهُمُ الرَّجْفَةُ فَاَصْبَحُوْا فِىْ دَارِهِمْ جٰثِمِيْنَ‏(37)\nFA-KAZZABOOHO FA-AKHAZATHOMUR RAJFATO FA-ASBAHOO FEE DAAREHIM JAASEMEEN.\nBut they belied him, so seized them an earthquake, and they lay (dead) in their abodes motionless.\nوَعَادًا وَّثَمُوْدَا۟ وَقَدْ تَّبَيَّنَ لَكُمْ مِّنْ مَّسٰكِنِهِمْ‌ وَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ الشَّيْطٰنُ اَعْمَالَهُمْ فَصَدَّهُمْ عَنِ السَّبِيْلِ وَكَانُوْا مُسْتَبْصِرِيْنَۙ‏(38)\nWA A’ADANW WA SAMOODAA WA QAT TABAYYANA LAKUM MIM MASAAKENEHIM, WA ZAYYANA LAHOMUSH SHAYTAANO A-A’MAALAHUM FA-SADDAHUM A’NIS SABEELE WA KAANOO MUSTABSEREEN.\nAnd We (destroyed) ’Ad and Thamud, and indeed it had been made manifest unto you from (the ruins of) their dwellings; and Satan made their deeds fair-seeming unto them, so he kept them back from the (right) path, though they were endued with sight,\nوَقَارُوْنَ وَفِرْعَوْنَ وَهَامٰنَ‌ وَلَقَدْ جَآءَهُمْ مُّوْسٰى بِالْبَيِّنٰتِ فَاسْتَكْبَرُوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَا كَانُوْا سٰبِقِيْنَ ‌ ۖ ‌ ۚ‏(39)\nWA QAAROONA WA FIR-A’WNA WA HAAMAAN, WA LAQAD JAAA-AHUM MOOSAA BIL-BAYYENAATE FAS-TAKBAROO FIL ARZE WA MAA KAANOO SAABEQEEN.\nAnd (We destroyed) Korah and Pharaoh and Haman: and indeed came unto them Moses with clear proofs but they behaved haughtily in the land, but they could not outstrip (Us).\nفَكُلًّا اَخَذْنَا بِذَنْۢبِهٖ‌ ۚ فَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ اَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِ حَاصِبًا‌ ۚ وَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ اَخَذَتْهُ الصَّيْحَةُ‌ ۚ وَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ خَسَفْنَا بِهِ الْاَرْضَ‌ ۚ وَمِنْهُمْ مَّنْ اَغْرَقْنَا‌ ۚ وَمَا كَانَ اللّٰهُ لِيَظْلِمَهُمْ وَلٰكِنْ كَانُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ يَظْلِمُوْنَ‏(40)\nFA-KULLAN AKHAZNAA BE-ZAMBEH, FAMINHUM MAN ARSALNAA A’LAYHE HAASEBAA, WA MINHUM MAN AKHAZATHUS SAYHAH, WA MINHUM MAN AGRAQNAA, WA MAA KAANAL LAAHO LE-YAZLEMAHUM WA LAAKIN KAANOO ANFOSAHUM YAZLEMOON.\nSo each (one of them) We did seize for his sin; and of them was he on whom We sent a stone-charged violent wind; and of them was he whom seized the blast; and of them was he whom We caused to be swallowed up by the earth; and of them was he whom We drowned; and it was not God to do injustice to them, but they unto their own selves did injustice,\nمَثَلُ الَّذِيْنَ اتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اَوْلِيَآءَ كَمَثَلِ الْعَنْكَبُوْتِ ‌ۖۚ اِتَّخَذَتْ بَيْتًا ‌ؕ وَ اِنَّ اَوْهَنَ الْبُيُوْتِ لَبَيْتُ الْعَنْكَبُوْتِ‌ۘ لَوْ كَانُوْا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(41)\nMASALUL LAZEENAT TAKHAZOO MIN DOONIL LAAHE AWLE-YAAA-A KAMASALIL A’NKABOOT, ITTAKHAZAT BAYTAA, WA INNA AWHANAL BOYOOTE LA-BAYTUL A’NKABOOT, LAW KAANOO YA’LAMOON.\nThe likeness of those who take to themselves guardians besides God, is the likeness of the spider that maketh for itself a house; but verily the frailest of all houses is the house of the spider; if they but know (this).\nاِنَّ اللّٰهَ يَعْلَمُ مَا يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ مِنْ شَىْءٍ‌ؕ وَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(42)\nINNAL LAAHA YA’LAMO MAA YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONEHI MIN SHAY, WA HOWAL A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nVerily, God knoweth whatever thing they call upon besides Him: and He is the All-Mighty, All-Wise.\nوَتِلْكَ الْاَمْثَالُ نَضْرِبُهَا لِلنَّاسِ‌ۚ وَمَا يَعْقِلُهَاۤ اِلَّا الْعٰلِمُوْنَ‏(43)\nWA TILKAL AMSAALO NAZREBOHAA LIN-NAAS, WA MAA YA’QELOHAA ILLAL A’ALEMOON.\nAnd these similitudes We do set forth unto people, but understand them none but the learned (ones)\nخَلَقَ اللّٰهُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَ الْاَرْضَ بِالْحَقِّ‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(44)\nKHALAQAL LAAHUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA BIL-HAQ, INNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYATAL LIL MOAMENEEN.\nGod created the heavens and the earth with truth; Verily in this there is a sign for the believers.\nاُتْلُ مَاۤ اُوْحِىَ اِلَيْكَ مِنَ الْكِتٰبِ وَاَقِمِ الصَّلٰوةَ ‌ؕ اِنَّ الصَّلٰوةَ تَنْهٰى عَنِ الْفَحْشَآءِ وَالْمُنْكَرِ‌ؕ وَلَذِكْرُ اللّٰهِ اَكْبَرُ‌ؕ وَاللّٰهُ يَعْلَمُ مَا تَصْنَعُوْنَ‏(45)\nUTLO MAAA OOHEYA ELAYKA MENAL KETAABE WA AQEMIS SALAAH, INNAS SALAATA TANHAA A’NIL FAHSHAAA-E WAL MUNKAR, WA LAZIKRUL LAAHE AKBAR, WAL LAAHO YA’LAMO MAA YASNA-O’ON.\nRecite thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) that which hath been revealed unto thee of the Book and establish prayer; verily prayer restraineth (one) from filth and evil; and certainly the remembrance of God is the greatest (duty of the believers), and God knoweth what ye do.\nوَلَا تُجَادِلُوْٓا اَهْلَ الْكِتٰبِ اِلَّا بِالَّتِىْ هِىَ اَحْسَنُۖ اِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا مِنْهُمْ‌ وَقُوْلُوْٓا اٰمَنَّا بِالَّذِىْۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْنَا وَاُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكُمْ وَاِلٰهُنَا وَاِلٰهُكُمْ وَاحِدٌ وَّنَحْنُ لَهٗ مُسْلِمُوْنَ‏(46)\nWA LAA TOJAADELOO AHLAL KETAABE ILLAA BIL-LATEE HEYA AHSAN, ILLAL LAZEENA ZALAMOO MINHUM WA QOOLOO AAMANNAA BIL-LAZEE UNZELA ELAYNAA WA UNZELA ELAYKUM WA ELAAHONAA WA ELAAHOKUM WAAHEDUNW WA NAHNO LAHU MUSLEMOON.\nAnd dispute not with the people of the Book save what is best, except those of them who act unjustly, and say ye (unto the people): “Believe we in that which hath been sent down unto us and sent down unto you, and our God and your God is One, and we unto Him do submit\nوَكَذٰلِكَ اَنْزَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبَ‌ؕ فَالَّذِيْنَ اٰتَيْنٰهُمُ الْكِتٰبَ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِهٖ‌ۚ وَمِنْ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ مَنْ يُّؤْمِنُ بِهٖ ‌ؕ وَ مَا يَجْحَدُ بِاٰيٰتِنَاۤ اِلَّا الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(47)\nWA KAZAALEKA ANZALNAA ELAYKAL KETAAB, FAL-LAZEENA AATAYNAAHOMUL KETAABA YOAMENOONA BEH, WA MIN HAA-OO-LAAA-E MANY YOAMENO BEH, WA MAA YAJHADO BE-AAYAATENAA ILLAL KAAFEROON.\nAnd thus have We sent down unto thee the Book (The Qur’an); and those whom We have given the Book believe in it; and of these there are those who believe in it; and dispute not against Our signs but the disbelievers.\nوَمَا كُنْتَ تَتْلُوْا مِنْ قَبْلِهٖ مِنْ كِتٰبٍ وَّلَا تَخُطُّهٗ بِيَمِيْنِكَ‌ اِذًا لَّارْتَابَ الْمُبْطِلُوْنَ‏(48)\nWA KUNTA TATLOO MIN QABLEHI MIN KETAABINW WA LAA TAKHUTTOHU BE-YAMEENEKA EZAL LARTAABAL MUBTELOON.\nAnd thou didst not recite any book before it (the Qur’an) and thou didst not transcribe one with that right hand of thine, for then would have doubted those who utter falsehood.\nبَلْ هُوَ اٰيٰتٌۢ بَيِّنٰتٌ فِىْ صُدُوْرِ الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْعِلْمَ‌ؕ وَمَا يَجْحَدُ بِاٰيٰتِنَاۤ اِلَّا الظّٰلِمُوْنَ‏(49)\nBAL HOWA AAYAATUM BAYYENAATUN FEE SODOORIL LAZEENA OOTUL I’LM, WA MAA YAJHADO BE-AAYAATENAA ILLAZ ZAALEMOON.\nNay! it (Qur’an) is the clear signs in the breast of those who have been granted the knowledge; and dispute not against Our signs except the unjust (ones)\nوَقَالُوْا لَوْلَاۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ اٰيٰتٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖ‌ؕ قُلْ اِنَّمَا الْاٰيٰتُ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَاِنَّمَاۤ اَنَا۟ نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(50)\nWA QAALOO LAWLAA UNZELA A’LAYHE AAYAATUM MIR RABBEH, QUL INNAMAL AAYAATO I’NDAL LAAH, WA INNAMAA ANAA NAZEERUM MOBEEN.\nAnd say they: “Why have not been sent down upon him the signs from the Lord?” Say thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “The signs are with God (alone); And I am only a plain warner\nاَوَلَمْ يَكْفِهِمْ اَنَّاۤ اَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْكَ الْكِتٰبَ يُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَرَحْمَةً وَّذِكْرٰى لِقَوْمٍ يُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(51)\nAWA LAM YAKFEHIM ANNAA ANZALNAA A’LAYKAL KETAABA YUTLAA A’LAYHIM, INNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-RAHMATANW WA ZIKRAA LEQAWMINY YOAMENOON.\nWhat! Is it not enough for them that We have sent down unto thee the Book which is recited unto them? Verily in this there is mercy and a reminder for a people who believe.\nقُلْ كَفٰى بِاللّٰهِ بَيْنِىْ وَبَيْنَكُمْ شَهِيْدًا ‌ۚ يَعْلَمُ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ ؕ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا بِالْبَاطِلِ وَكَفَرُوْا بِاللّٰهِ ۙ اُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْخٰسِرُوْنَ‏(52)\nQUL KAFAA BIL LAAHE BAYNEE WA BAYNAKUM SHAHEEDAA, YA’LAMO MAA FIS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ, WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO BIL-BAATELE WA KAFAROO BIL LAAHE, OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL KHAASEROON.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!): “Sufficient is God as a witness between me and you; He knoweth what is in the heavens and the earth; and those who believe in the falsehood and disbelieve in God; these it is who are the losers.\nوَيَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَكَ بِالْعَذَابِ‌ؕ وَلَوْلَاۤ اَجَلٌ مُّسَمًّى لَّجَآءَهُمُ الْعَذَابُؕ وَلَيَاْتِيَنَّهُمْ بَغْتَةً وَّهُمْ لَا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(53)\nWA YASTA’JELOONAKA BIL A’ZAAB, WA LAW LAA AJALUM MOSAMMAAL LA-JAAA-AHOMUL A’ZAAB, WA LAYAATEYANNAHUM BAGHTATANW WA HUM LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nAnd they challenge thee to hasten on the chastisement; and had not the term been decreed, the chastisement would certainly have come unto them; and certainly, it will come unto them suddenly while they perceive not.\nيَسْتَعْجِلُوْنَكَ بِالْعَذَابِؕ وَ اِنَّ جَهَنَّمَ لَمُحِيْطَةٌۢ بِالْكٰفِرِيْنَۙ‏(54)\nYASTA’JELOONAKA BIL-A’ZAAB, WA INNA JAHANNAMA LA-MOHEETATUM BIL-KAAFEREEN.\nAnd they challenge thee to hasten on the chastisement, and verily the Hell will encompass the disbelievers,\nيَوْمَ يَغْشٰٮهُمُ الْعَذَابُ مِنْ فَوْقِهِمْ وَمِنْ تَحْتِ اَرْجُلِهِمْ وَيَقُوْلُ ذُوْقُوْا مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(55)\nYAWMA YAGHSHAA-HOMUL A’ZAABO MIN FAWQEHIM WA MIN TAHTE ARJOLEHIM WA YAQOOLO ZOOQOO MAA KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nOn the day when shall cover them the chastisement, from above them, and from beneath their feet; and shall say He; “Taste ye what ye were doing.\nيٰعِبَادِىَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْۤا اِنَّ اَرْضِىْ وَاسِعَةٌ فَاِيَّاىَ فَاعْبُدُوْنِ‏(56)\nYAA E’BAADEYAL LAZEENA AAMANOO INNA ARZEE WAASE-A’TUN FA-IYYAA-YA FA’BODOON.\nO’ My servants who believe! verily My earth is vast, therefore Me alone should ye worship!\nكُلُّ نَفْسٍ ذَآئِقَةُ الْمَوْتِ ثُمَّ اِلَيْنَا تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(57)\nKULLO NAFSIN ZAAA-EQATUL MAWT, SUMMA ELAYNAA TURJA-O’ON.\nEvery soul shall taste of death; Then unto Us (only) ye shall (all) be returned.\nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوْا الصّٰلِحٰتِ لَنُبَوِّئَنَّهُمْ مِّنَ الْجَنَّةِ غُرَفًا تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا ‌ؕ نِعْمَ اَجْرُ الْعٰمِلِيْنَ‌ۖ‏(58)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE LA-NOBAWWE-ANNAHUM MENAL JANNATE GHORAFAN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA, NE’MA AJRUL A’AMELEENAL.\nAnd those who believe and do good, certainly will We lodge them in the exalted places in the gardens beneath which flow rivers, they shall abide therein; How excellent is the recompense of those who act (aright),\nالَّذِيْنَ صَبَرُوْا وَعَلٰى رَبِّهِمْ يَتَوَكَّلُوْنَ‏(59)\nLAZEENA SABAROO WA A’LAA RABBEHIM YATAWAKKALOON.\nThose who are steadfast and, on their Lord, do they rely,\nوَكَاَيِّنْ مِّنْ دَآبَّةٍ لَّا تَحْمِلُ رِزْقَهَاۖ اللّٰهُ يَرْزُقُهَا وَاِيَّاكُمْ‌‌ۖ وَهُوَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(60)\nWA KA-AYYIM MIN DAAAB-BATIL LAA TAHMELO RIZQAHAA, ALLAAHO YARZOQOHAA WA IYYAAKUM, WA HOWAS SAMEE-U’L A’LEEM.\nAnd how many a moving creature that doth not carry its sustenance; God sustaineth it and yourselves; And He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.\nوَلَئِنْ سَاَلْتَهُمْ مَّنْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَسَخَّرَ الشَّمْسَ وَالْقَمَرَ لَيَقُوْلُنَّ اللّٰهُ‌ۚ فَاَنّٰى يُؤْفَكُوْنَ‏(61)\nWA LAIN SA-ALTAHUM MAN KHALAQAS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA SAKHKHARASH SHAMSA WAL QAMARA LAYAQOOLUNNAL LAAH, FA-ANNAA YOAFEKOON.\nAnd if thou ask them: “Who created the heavens and the earth and made subservient the sun and the moon?” Certainly will they say: “God!” Whence are they then turned away?\nاَللّٰهُ يَبْسُطُ الرِّزْقَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖ وَيَقْدِرُ لَهٗ ؕ اِنَّ اللّٰهَ بِكُلِّ شَىْءٍ عَلِيْمٌ‏(62)\nALLAAHO YABSOTUR RIZQA LEMANY YASHAAA-O MIN E’BAADEHI WA YAQDERO LAH, INNAL LAAHA BEKULLE SHAYIN A’LEEM.\nGod (it is Who) maketh abundant the sustenance for whomsoever He willeth of His servants, and (similarly) He causeth it to be straitened for him (whomsoever He willeth); Verily God is Well-Cognizant of all things.\nوَلَئِنْ سَاَلْتَهُمْ مَّنْ نَّزَّلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً فَاَحْيَا بِهِ الْاَرْضَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَوْتِهَا لَيَقُوْلُنَّ اللّٰهُ‌ؕ قُلِ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ‌ؕ بَلْ اَكْثَرُهُمْ لَا يَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(63)\nWA LAIN SA-ALTAHUM AMN NAZZALA MENAS SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FA-AHYAA BEHIL ARZA MIM BA’DE MAWTEHAA LAYAQOOLUNNAL LAAH, QOLIL HAMDO LILLAAH, BAL AKSAROHUM LAA YA’QELOON.\nAnd if thou ask them, “Who sendeth down from heaven the water, and giveth life with it unto the earth after its death?” Certainly, will they say: “God!” Say, “all praise is His;” Nay! most of them understand not.\nوَمَا هٰذِهِ الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَاۤ اِلَّا لَهْوٌ وَّلَعِبٌ‌ؕ وَاِنَّ الدَّارَ الْاٰخِرَةَ لَهِىَ الْحَيَوَانُ‌ۘ لَوْ كَانُوْا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(64)\nWA MAA HAAZEHIL HAYAATUD DUNYAA ILLAA LAHWUNW WA LA-E’B, WA INNAD DAARAL AAKHERATA LAHEYAL HAYAWAAN, LAW KAANOO YA’LAMOON.\nAnd nothing is this life of the world but a vain sport and play; and verily the abode of the hereafter, is certainly the life: if they but know.\nفَاِذَا رَكِبُوْا فِى الْفُلْكِ دَعَوُا اللّٰهَ مُخْلِصِيْنَ لَهُ الدِّيْنَ ۚ فَلَمَّا نَجّٰٮهُمْ اِلَى الْبَرِّ اِذَا هُمْ يُشْرِكُوْنَۙ‏(65)\nFA-EZAA RAKEBOO FIL FULKE DA-A’WUL LAAHA MUKHLESEENA LAHUD DEEN, FALAMMAA NAJJAAHUM ELAL BARRE EZAA HUM YUSHREKOONA.\nAnd when embark they on ships, call they upon God sincerely vowing worship (only) unto Him, and when He bringeth them safe to land, behold! they associate (others with Him),\nلِيَكْفُرُوْا بِمَاۤ اٰتَيْنٰهُمْۙۚ وَلِيَتَمَتَّعُوْا‌فَسَوْفَ يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(66)\nLE-YAKFOROO BEMAA AATAYNAAHUM, WA LE-YATAMATTA-O’O, FA-SAWFA YA’LAMOON.\n(Then) let them thank not for what We have given them, and let them enjoy; but soon shall they know.\nاَوَلَمْ يَرَوْا اَنَّا جَعَلْنَا حَرَمًا اٰمِنًا وَّيُتَخَطَّفُ النَّاسُ مِنْ حَوْلِهِمْ‌ ؕ اَفَبِالْبَاطِلِ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ وَبِنِعْمَةِ اللّٰهِ يَكْفُرُوْنَ‏(67)\nAWA LAM YARAW ANNAA JA-A’LNAA HARAMAN AAMENANW WA YOTAKHATTAFUN NAASO MIN HAWLEHIM, AFA-BIL-BAATELE YOAMENOONA WA BE-NE’MATIL LAAHE YAKFOROON.\nWhat! See they not that We have established a Sacred Precinct Secure, while people are ravaged all around them? Will they yet believe in the falsehood and in the bounty of God disbelieve?\nوَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ افْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا اَوْ كَذَّبَ بِالْحَقِّ لَمَّا جَآءَهٗ‌ؕ اَلَيْسَ فِىْ جَهَنَّمَ مَثْوًى لِّلْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(68)\nWA MAN AZLAMO MIMMANIF TARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN AW KAZZABA BIL-HAQQE LAMMAA JAAA-AH, A-LAYSA FEE JAHANNAMA MASWAL LIL-KAAFEREEN.\nAnd who is more unjust than he who forgeth a lie against God, or belieth the truth when it hath come unto him? Is not in the Hell the abode for the disbelievers?\nوَالَّذِيْنَ جَاهَدُوْا فِيْنَا لَنَهْدِيَنَّهُمْ سُبُلَنَا ‌ؕ وَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَمَعَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(69)\nWAL LAZEENA JAAHADOO FEENAA LA-NAHDEYANNAHUM SOBOLANAA, WA INNAL LAAHA LA-MA-A’L MOHSENEEN.\nAnd those who strive hard in Us, certainly will We guide them in Our ways; And verily God is (always) with those who do good.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Ankaboot (The Spider)\nThe first 11 verses of this Surah are ‘Madani’ and the rest were revealed in Makkah. This Surah has a total of 69 verses. In the commentary of Burhan it is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recites Surah al-Ankaboot on the 23rd night of the month of Ramazan, will enter Paradise without any questioning.\nThe Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the reward for reciting this Surah can be compared to ten times the number of believing men and women plus ten times the number of hypocrites on Earth. Drinking water in which this Surah has been dissolved brings one great joy and happiness in his life."
}
